<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cesare Borgia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1475">1475</a>–<a href="/years/1507">1507</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Duke Valentino</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cesare Borgia was the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-alexander-vi">Pope Alexander VI</a>. Made Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valentinois">Valentinois</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xii-of-france">Louis XII of France</a> in 1498, he used papal money and French troops to conquer the lordships of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romagna">Romagna</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marche">Marche</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imola">Imola</a>, Forlì, Rimini, Pesaro, Faenza and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camerino">Camerino</a>, forming a Duchy of Romagna. His state collapsed after his father's death in 1503, and he was killed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cesare-borgia.jpg" alt="Cesare Borgia" width="320" height="421" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: After Bartolomeo Veneto · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cesare_Borgia,_Duke_of_Valentinois.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
